    <item>
      <headword id="idp118871128">“keppar”</headword>
      <description>a “piece” to a boy or girl. (Stoer, Assynt) The “keppar” always consisted of a scone (flour) for preference or an oatcake with fresh butter and at least an inch of crowdie. “Hor ‘keppar’ dhan a bhallach!” – usually if the housewife was baking.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp118873000">[breacag nan</headword>
      <description>[?] eorna] “Breacag nan [?] eorna nach eil solar na fallain.” Part of a New Year duan – the thin barley bannock was not appreciated. They would accept anything except that!</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp118874728">“mear”</headword>
